><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250523105131+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250523105146+10'00'" name="21b107d1-0719-4f7f-a98c-619f4db9b541" page="10" coords="509.154877,240.626404,568.519897,240.626404,509.154877,229.466583,568.519897,229.466583,316.500000,229.524384,568.516724,229.524384,316.500000,218.364563,568.516724,218.364563,316.500000,218.422394,568.537537,218.422394,316.500000,207.262573,568.537537,207.262573,316.500000,207.320374,568.524902,207.320374,316.500000,196.160553,568.524902,196.160553,316.500000,196.218384,568.541260,196.218384,316.500000,185.058563,568.541260,185.058563,316.500000,185.116364,568.525146,185.116364,316.500000,173.956543,568.525146,173.956543,316.500000,174.014374,568.513428,174.014374,316.500000,162.854553,568.513428,162.854553,316.500000,162.912354,568.518738,162.912354,316.500000,151.752533,568.518738,151.752533,316.500000,151.810364,568.521484,151.810364,316.500000,140.650543,568.521484,140.650543,316.500000,140.708344,568.540344,140.708344,316.500000,129.548523,568.540344,129.548523,316.500000,129.606354,568.513855,129.606354,316.500000,118.446533,568.513855,118.446533,316.500000,118.504349,568.523071,118.504349,316.500000,107.344528,568.523071,107.344528,316.500000,107.402359,568.517822,107.402359,316.500000,96.242538,568.517822,96.242538,316.500000,96.300354,568.520264,96.300354,316.500000,85.140533,568.520264,85.140533,316.500000,85.198364,568.530273,85.198364,316.500000,74.038544,568.530273,74.038544,316.500000,74.096359,568.510010,74.096359,316.500000,62.936539,568.510010,62.936539,316.500000,62.994354,568.505737,62.994354,316.500000,51.834534,568.505737,51.834534" rect="316.151245,51.485779,568.890015,240.975159" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
> It is also&#xD;recommended in future studies to verify ROI selection with a&#xD;second assessor, as previously seen when tracing muscle&#xD;boundaries to calculate CSA in cervical musculature (36).&#xD;Verification of ROI selection by a second assessor was not&#xD;mentioned in any of the studies included in this review.&#xD;Appropriate ROI selection is an important factor for T2 relaxometry&#xD;value calculation, as different values are characteristic&#xD;of different tissues (29). Therefore, the accidental inclusion of&#xD;fat, blood vessels, aponeurosis, bone, and tendon in a ROI will&#xD;affect T2 relaxometry values. ROI selection should be verified&#xD;by a second assessor and reliability of ROI selection reported.&#xD;Lastly, to capture peak T2 relaxometry values, the time between&#xD;exercise cessation and scan acquisition completion&#xD;should be kept to a minimum by adjusting MRI scan acquisition&#xD;time and exercise protocol type and location. Considerations&#xD;should also be made regarding the number of TE </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>included within the scanning parameters, as this affects both&#xD;scan acquisition time and T2 relaxation value calculations.</span
></p
